# VSCO Workspace integration — resolved studio IDs.
#
# We DO commit apps/site/vsco-config.json so production deploys have the
# file available without needing to run the bootstrap inside the container.
# The contents are non-secret (ULIDs that identify lookup entries in the
# studio); only VSCO_API_KEY is sensitive and it lives in env vars.
#
# If you regenerate the config (e.g. you re-bootstrap a fresh studio), the
# resulting file should be committed. The bootstrap script is idempotent
# and re-running it against an already-configured studio produces an
# equivalent file with the same ULIDs.

